I am trying to develop a GUI application with the STM32H7S78-DK.  I want to send uart data from the board over wires to a raspberry pi.  To simplify the process without graphics I'm just trying to send a simple "Hello" string over UART7.  From what I can see from the data sheet, UART7 is connected to pins PE7 and PE8, which correspond to D0 and D1 on CN14 on the arduino headers by default.  Please correct me if I am wrong.  So I first am just initializing those pins with uart on STM32CubeMX then I was just sending a simple HAL\_UART\_Transmit() with a 2 second HAL\_Delay().  However, I see no data coming through when putting a logic analyzer on those pins. What am I doing wrong?

